//! tr kodlu 1
// 01 — Hello: the first TR program.
// What it teaches: writing to the screen with print, string literals, several values, line breaks and comments.
// Builds on: — (the first example).
// Run (from the project root): tr examples/en/01_hello.tr
// For your own experiments you can copy this file into the scratch/ folder and change it
// (scratch/ stays out of the repository).

// A line that starts with two slashes is a comment: the program skips it, it is a note to the reader.
G100("Hello, world!")
G100("This is the second line.")

// Values separated by commas are written on the same line, with a space between them.
G100("Three", "values", "side by side")
G100(2026) // a number can be printed too; quotes are only for text

// \n inside a string means a line break.
G100("First line\nSecond line")

// --- Try it yourself ---
// 1. Print a greeting with your own name.
// 2. Instead of three separate prints, write three strings in a single print.
